-- title:
--   Positive prefix mass forces a valid reporting prefix
-- statement:
--   Let $\alpha,\beta,\gamma$ be finite index types with decidable equality, and let $I$ be a finite set of raw items for block parameters $h,J$. Fix a wanted label $w=(a,\ell,q)$ and a natural number $k\le J$. For a list $P$ of subsets of $\{0,\ldots,512h-1\}$, let $F(I,w,k,P)$ count the raw items in $I$ whose wanted label is $w$ and whose partition word begins with exactly $P$ as its first $k$ entries. If $Q_j$ is the output subset in block $j$ of $q$, then
--   $$F(I,w,k,P)>0\quad\Longrightarrow\quad |P|=k\ \land\ \forall j<k,\ P_j\subseteq Q_j\ \land\ |P_j|=h.$$
--
--   Consequently, a malformed prefix cannot carry positive raw-incidence mass.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/StoredReporting.lean#L79-L96

